W:1.Round goes the wheel of fortune, don't be afraid to ride,
W:There's a land of milk and honey, lies on the other side,
W:There'll be peace and there'll be plenty, you'll never need to roam,
W:When we go rolling home, when we go rolling home.
W:Ch. Rolling home, when we go, rolling home, when we go,
W:Rolling, rolling, when we go rolling home.
W:2. The gentry in their finery do prosper night and morn,
W:While we into the fields must go, to plough and sow their corn,
W:The rich, they steal the power, but the glory's ours alone,
W:When we go rolling home, when we go rolling home.
W:3.The frost is on the hedgerows, the icy winds do blow,
W:While we poor weary labourers, strive through the driving snow,
W:Our dreams fly up to glory, up where the lark has flown,
W:When we go rolling home, when we go rolling home.
W:4.The summer of resentment, the winter of despair,
W:The journey to contentment is set with trap and snare,
W:Stand true and stand together, your labour's all your own,
W:When you go rolling home, when you go rolling home.
W:5.So pass the bottle round, and let the toast go free,
W:Here's a health to every labourer, wherever they may be,
W:Fair wages now and ever, let's reap what we have sown,
W:When we go rolling home, when we go rolling home.
W:[Chorus with instruments - as with earlier verses]
W:[Chorus sung acapellawith (no instruments)] 
W:[Final chorus with instruments]